# Mizani build rules

You are building Mizani, an agent that prepares cited procurement briefs from Kenya OCDS data for a human committee.

## Non-negotiables

- The agent never awards a tender, ranks bidders or recommends a winner. No tool for this may exist.
- Approval is NOT an MCP tool and is not reachable by the model. It is a separate CLI command that records a named approver.
- Every finding carries a non-empty list of record IDs. Reject findings without them in the schema.
- All numbers in findings come from deterministic code. The model never computes them.
- Never use live tenders or personal details. Company and buyer records only.
- Write all code fresh. Do not copy code from any earlier project.
- Never invent threshold values. Read them from config/thresholds.yaml, each with a legal_source.

## Code quality

- Python 3.11+, type hints everywhere, Pydantic v2 models for all tool inputs and outputs.
- Module docstring on every file; docstring on every function (inputs, outputs, why).
- Keep functions small and single-purpose. No dead code.
- Format and lint with ruff. Add pytest tests beside each module.
- Log every tool call through the ledger wrapper, not inside the tool.

## Build order (do not skip ahead)

1. Repo scaffold, Makefile, config, licence
2. Ingestion: OCDS loader, filters, canonicalisation, DuckDB, data-quality report
3. Ledger
4. Detectors
5. Verifier
6. MCP server (five core tools)
7. LangGraph agent
8. Brief generator and approval CLI
9. Eval harness E1–E12
10. README, ARCHITECTURE.md, demo
11. Stretch only after core passes

## When unsure

Ask before guessing about data fields, endpoint formats or legal thresholds.
